W: Chorus:
W: Gather up the pots and the old tin can,
W: The mash, the corn, the barley and the bran,
W: Run like the devil from the excise man,
W: Keep the smoke from rising Barney.
W:
W: 1. Keep your eyes well-peeled today,
W: The big tall men are on their way,
W: Searching for the mountain tay,
W: In the hills of Connemara.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 2. Mountain breezes as they blow,
W: Hear their echo in the glens below,
W: The gombeen men are on the go,
W: In the hills of Connemara.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 3. A gallon for the butcher, a quart for Tom,
W: A bottle for poor old Father John,
W: To help his prayers and hymns along,
W: In the hills of Connemara.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. Stand your ground boys, it’s too late!
W: The excise men are at the gate,
W: Glory be to God, they’re drinkin' it straight,
W: In the hills of Connemara.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 5. Swing to the left and swing to the right,
W: The excise men will dance all night,
W: Drinkin' up the tay till the broad daylight,
W: In the hills of Connemara.
W: (Chorus)
